How they line up against SSPS / Mint‑to Logic
x402 ≈ Mint‑to payment substrate (validation‑gated routing of value and access).

EVMAuth ≈ SSPS licensing / entitlement / TTL layer (who may do what, for how long, with what credits).

AWS Secrets / STS ≈ traditional infra‑secrets & identity substrate that SSPS can wrap or replace in certain verticals.

AgentKit ≈ agent runtime & orchestration, where SSPS governs which agents, which tools, and which payment/auth rails are allowed.

Zenity ≈ runtime governance / guardrail hardening, closer to SSPS’s stabilization and compliance primitives around agent behavior.

If you want, next step is to turn this into a stack diagram: SSPS at the top as governance/continuity, with x402 + EVMAuth as economic/auth substrates, AWS as legacy infra, and AgentKit + Zenity as the agent runtime and enforcement band.
